.TH EITAAS 1 "August 2026" "EITaaS-Linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eitaas \- diagnose and launch community AVD connections with smart-card redirection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eitaas doctor
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas inspect-profile
.I FILE
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas smartcard status
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas connect
.I FILE
.br
.B eitaas certificates
.RI { fetch | inspect }
.SH DESCRIPTION
EITaaS-Linux is an independent community helper for diagnosing and launching
Azure Virtual Desktop connections through the bundled one-shot
.BR eitaas-remmina (1)
client, an isolated Remmina and FreeRDP pair installed under a private prefix.
.PP
.B eitaas connect
validates the profile (regular file, owned by the caller, mode 0600, at most
1 MiB, .rdpw extension) and then runs
.B eitaas-remmina FILE
with no other arguments, no shell, and no inherited standard streams. It does
not construct RDP or authentication arguments; all connection policy is
applied inside the bundled client.
.PP
It does not disable certificate verification, request a CAC PIN, or install
polkit rules or certificate trust anchors during ordinary operation.
.SH SECURITY
Connection profiles must be regular files owned by the current user without
group or other permissions. Use chmod 600 on a downloaded profile before use.
.PP
Clipboard redirection has no switch in
.BR eitaas .
The bundled client follows the profile's
.B redirectclipboard
field through Remmina's RDPW importer; a profile that omits the field gets the
RDP default (enabled). This is by design: the exported profile is the policy
source, and the launcher does not override it. The field is not forwarded to
FreeRDP's native profile parser.
.PP
Never publish real RDP/RDPW files or authentication callback URLs. See the
installed SECURITY.md documentation for reporting guidance.
.PP
Authentication uses either the Microsoft Identity Broker (when the bundle was
built with SSO-MIB) or the embedded CAC WebView; the terminal URL/callback
fallback is refused inside the bundled client.
.SH DOCTOR
.B eitaas doctor
reports whether
.B eitaas-remmina
is on PATH, whether the private client binary exists under
.I /usr/libexec/eitaas-remmina
or
.IR /usr/lib/eitaas-remmina ,
the pinned Remmina and FreeRDP versions from the installed
.I sources.json
manifest (or "unknown"), whether the installed FreeRDP client library links
SSO-MIB, identity-broker registration on the session bus, the PC/SC socket,
and the presence of smart-card tools. Readiness requires the launcher, the
private client, and healthy smart-card checks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. One indicates completed diagnostics with unmet
requirements. Two indicates invalid input or an operation error. A connection
otherwise returns the exit status of the
.B eitaas-remmina
child.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcsc_scan (1),
.BR pkcs11-tool (1),
.BR remmina (1)
